tasks.description:
Review the Facebook content calendar below against the brand guidelines.

Brand Identity: {brand_identity}
Brand Pillars: {brand_pillars}
Target Audience: {target_audience}
Core Goals: {core_goals}
Posting Ratio & Calendar:
{calendar_output}

For each post entry, check:
1. Brand voice consistency \ u2014 does the topic match the brand tone and identity?
2. Pillar balance \ u2014 does the overall distribution respect the approved posting ratio?
3. Completeness \ u2014 are all required fields present (post_id, date, time, pillar, topic, target_audience, goal, cta_type, visual_brief_concept, status)?
4. Status field \ u2014 is every entry's status set to 'Idea'?

List all flagged issues clearly. If no issues are found, state 'All entries passed review.'
If the calendar input contains NO DATA, output: NO DATA: calendar generation returned nothing

Review the following brand inputs and define a balanced weekly content posting ratio across the brand pillars for Facebook.

Brand Identity: {brand_identity}
Brand Pillars: {brand_pillars}
Target Audience: {target_audience}
Core Goals: {core_goals}
Target Period: {target_period}

Deliverables:
1. A percentage-based posting ratio across all pillars (e.g. 40% Value, 30% Engagement, 20% Product/Sales, 10% Brand Story).
2. A brief rationale for each pillar's weight based on the stated core goals.
3. A recommended posting frequency per week (e.g. 5 posts/week).

Base your output strictly on the provided inputs. If a required input is missing or empty, output: NO DATA: brand inputs returned nothing
